    <p>These Terms of Service ("Terms") form a legal agreement between you ("Client," "you," "your") and Tycoon Clap ("we," "us," "our"), the operator of tycoonclap.com (the "Site"). They apply to the Site and to every service and product we provide, including Growth Marketing (performance marketing and paid media), Software Engineering (web and mobile app development), Data &amp; AI (data analytics and business intelligence), and our verified B2B lead lists (together, the "Services").</p>

    <h2 id="acceptance">1. Acceptance of these Terms</h2>
    <p>By accessing the Site, requesting a proposal, signing a statement of work, making a payment, or otherwise using the Services, you confirm that you have read and agree to these Terms, our <a href="privacy-policy.html">Privacy Policy</a>, and our <a href="cancellation-refund-policy.html">Cancellation &amp; Refund Policy</a>. If you are accepting on behalf of a company, you confirm that you have authority to bind that company.</p>
    <p>If a signed proposal, statement of work, or master services agreement ("Engagement Document") conflicts with these Terms, the Engagement Document prevails for that engagement.</p>

    <h2 id="services">2. Our Services and how engagements work</h2>
    <h3>2.1 Proposals and scope</h3>
    <p>Each engagement is defined by a written proposal, quote, or statement of work that sets out the deliverables, timelines, fees, and any assumptions. Work outside the agreed scope is handled as a change request and may be charged separately. We will confirm any scope or price change with you in writing before starting that work.</p>

    <h3>2.2 Service categories</h3>
    <table class="data-table">
      <tr><th>Service</th><th>What it typically includes</th><th>Commercial model</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Growth Marketing</td><td>Paid media (Google, Meta and similar), landing pages, tracking setup, reporting, optimization</td><td>Monthly retainer; ad spend billed separately by the ad platform</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Software Engineering</td><td>Websites, web apps, mobile apps, integrations, maintenance</td><td>Fixed-price project with milestones, or time &amp; materials</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Data &amp; AI</td><td>Data pipelines, dashboards (e.g. Power BI), analytics, automation</td><td>Fixed-price project or monthly retainer</td></tr>
      <tr><td>B2B Lead Lists</td><td>Verified contact data delivered as a digital file</td><td>One-time purchase via the Leads page</td></tr>
    </table>

    <h3>2.3 Timelines</h3>
    <p>Dates in a proposal are good-faith estimates. They depend on timely feedback, access, content, and approvals from you. Delays caused by missing inputs, late payments, or changes in scope may move delivery dates.</p>

    <h2 id="fees">3. Fees, invoicing, and payment</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Fees:</strong> Fees are as stated in your proposal, order, or the price shown on the Leads page at checkout.</li>
      <li><strong>Invoicing:</strong> Retainers are invoiced in advance for the coming period. Project work is invoiced by milestone, or as stated in the proposal. Unless otherwise agreed, invoices are due within 7 days of the invoice date.</li>
      <li><strong>Payment methods:</strong> We accept payment through PayPal, Stripe, and bank transfer where offered. Card and PayPal details are processed entirely by those providers; we do not receive or store them.</li>
      <li><strong>Currency and taxes:</strong> Fees are quoted in the currency stated on the proposal or checkout page. Fees are exclusive of applicable taxes (such as GST, VAT, or sales tax) unless stated otherwise. You are responsible for taxes and for any bank, currency-conversion, or payment-processor charges on your side.</li>
      <li><strong>Late payment:</strong> If an invoice is overdue, we may pause work, withhold deliverables or access, and charge reasonable interest on the overdue amount, after giving you written notice.</li>
      <li><strong>Refunds and cancellations:</strong> These are governed by our <a href="cancellation-refund-policy.html">Cancellation &amp; Refund Policy</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="client">4. Your responsibilities</h2>
    <p>To deliver good results, we depend on you to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Provide accurate information, content, brand assets, and timely access to accounts, platforms, and systems we need (for example ad accounts, analytics, hosting, and source data).</li>
      <li>Review and approve deliverables within the timeframe agreed in the proposal, or within 5 business days if none is stated.</li>
      <li>Make sure that you own or have the right to use all materials you give us, and that they do not infringe anyone's rights or break the law.</li>
      <li>Keep your account credentials secure and tell us promptly of any suspected unauthorised access.</li>
      <li>Comply with all laws that apply to your business, products, advertising claims, and marketing activity.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="platforms">5. Third-party platforms, tools, and ad spend</h2>
    <p>Our Services rely on third-party platforms such as Google, Meta, Microsoft, payment processors, hosting providers, and analytics tools. We do not control these platforms and are not responsible for their outages, policy changes, account suspensions, ad disapprovals, pricing changes, or algorithm updates.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Ad spend is separate.</strong> Advertising budgets are paid by you directly to the ad platform and are not included in our fees unless the proposal says otherwise.</li>
      <li><strong>Account ownership.</strong> Ad accounts, analytics properties, and similar assets created for your business should be held in your name. We will request the access levels needed to operate them.</li>
      <li><strong>Third-party costs.</strong> Software licences, hosting, domains, stock assets, and similar costs are billed at cost or as stated in the proposal.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="leads">6. B2B lead lists</h2>
